Fix WTT - Pack 'n' Strap 2.0.4
The WTT-PackNStrap 2.0.4 source was modified to prevent the mod from interfering with SPT's insurance system.

The change in WTTPackNStrap.cs consists of removing the activation of HandleInsuredItemLostEventPatch.

Before:
new HandleInsuredItemLostEventPatch().Enable();

After:
The line is removed.

IsItemKeptAfterDeathPatch remains enabled, so PackNStrap keeps its functionality related to items that should be retained after death.

The HandleInsuredItemLostEventPatch.cs file is not deleted from the project; it is simply no longer enabled.

This allows PackNStrap to continue providing its items and functionality while leaving the processing of insured items entirely to SPT's vanilla Insurance system.

Result:

PackNStrap → mod items and functionality.

SPT InsuranceService → insurance management.

SPT's vanilla insurance behavior is not modified.
This is the explanation what I've done in WTT-PackNStrap.dll 
The DLL was changed to stop PackNStrap from modifying SPT's insurance system.

The HandleInsuredItemLostEventPatch is no longer enabled by the DLL.

The rest of PackNStrap remains unchanged. The mod items, belts, containers, and IsItemKeptAfterDeathPatch still work normally.

This means SPT handles insurance normally, without PackNStrap changing the insured items after a raid and stop blocking the game. 
